/-!
# Component extension in the fixed-line centralizer

The actual star marking and supplied module-centralizer equality identify
L/O₂(L) with A₈ and force S to induce a non-inner automorphism on this section.
Once L is a normal C-component of C_G(Z₁), the centerless argument behind
A.3.18 identifies L with the subgroup generated by its three-power elements.

The remaining extension reduction must specialize the full A.3.12 embedding
list, transport the genuine parabolic and local-component hypotheses, and
apply the L₅(2), M₂₄ and J₄ stabilizer calculations. In particular the J₄
stabilizer is still under development in Chapter 1. This module does not yet
assert 15.3.32(3); the conditional residual adapter records the placement
premises that the extension argument must discharge.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004),
15.3.32(3), printed pp.1132–1133; 1.2.4, p.505; A.3.12 and A.3.18,
pp.47–48 and 51–52.
-/
